threads.body:
[Testing] If the reduced matrix stays, please express it as data on `@AppServer` rather than as reflection plus an `instanceof` chain in the base class. The matrix already lives on the annotation; the reduced subset is just another column of it.

Add to `AppServer.java`:

```java
  boolean reduced() default false;
```

then mark the ~54 nested classes that make up the reduced set, and this whole block collapses to:

```suggestion
    // In reduced mode (PR builds), only run a representative subset of the full matrix.
    // The full matrix runs on merge to main.
    assumeTrue(appServer.reduced() || !Boolean.getBoolean("reducedSmokeTests"));
```

That's ~45 lines deleted (see my comment below), no reflection, no base class referencing its own subclasses, and — the part I care most about — which cases run on a PR becomes visible in the diff whenever someone adds a server version or a JDK, instead of being silently derived by a rule they never see.

